# XCU pwd
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Tests run in the private directory the driver gives. Scaffolding uses only POSIX utilities; setup problems are UNRESOLVED.

assertion  XCU.pwd.001
anchor     utilities/pwd.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/pwd.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.6
class      required
says       pwd writes one line with an absolute pathname of the current
           directory that has no dot or dot-dot components and no needless
           slashes, both as the shell runs it and by a direct exec.
test       t/001-plain.sh

assertion  XCU.pwd.002
anchor     utilities/pwd.html#OPTIONS
class      required
says       pwd -P writes the physical directory: no component that is a
           symbolic link.
test       t/002-option-P.sh

assertion  XCU.pwd.003
anchor     utilities/pwd.html#OPTIONS
class      required
says       pwd -L, and pwd without options, write the PWD pathname when it
           is valid, so a path through a symbolic link is kept.
note       The shell sets PWD when it changes directory; the test only
           exports it for the direct exec and never assigns a value.
test       t/003-option-L.sh

assertion  XCU.pwd.004
anchor     utilities/pwd.html#OPTIONS
class      required
says       When both -L and -P are given the last one applies.
test       t/004-L-P-last.sh
